WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:09.679
The lion was very strong.

2
00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:13.786
He was the king of all the other animals.

3
00:00:13.787 --> 00:00:16.984
One day the lion met a monkey.

4
00:00:16.985 --> 00:00:19.715
"Good morning, Your Majesty!

5
00:00:19.716 --> 00:00:23.655
Your mane looks wonderful today," said the monkey.

6
00:00:23.656 --> 00:00:27.115
"Of course!" agreed the lion.

7
00:00:27.116 --> 00:00:33.813
Suddenly the monkey held his nose, "Oh my!"

8
00:00:33.814 --> 00:00:38.634
"Is something wrong, little monkey?" asked the lion.

9
00:00:38.635 --> 00:00:42.376
"Uh, no, no. Nothing, sir."

10
00:00:42.377 --> 00:00:45.445
"Then why did you make such a face?

11
00:00:45.446 --> 00:00:49.186
Tell me the truth!" the lion commanded.

12
00:00:49.187 --> 00:00:52.944
"Well, uh," the monkey trembled.

13
00:00:52.945 --> 00:00:57.996
"Your breath smells bad. That's all."

14
00:00:57.997 --> 00:01:00.692
"My breath smells bad?

15
00:01:00.693 --> 00:01:04.100
Is that all?" repeated the lion.

16
00:01:04.101 --> 00:01:06.699
"Oh yes! Yes, that's it.

17
00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:09.691
That's all!" said the monkey.

18
00:01:09.692 --> 00:01:14.026
"Okay, then you will never smell it again!"

19
00:01:14.027 --> 00:01:18.107
And the lion ate the monkey up.

20
00:01:18.108 --> 00:01:20.824
The lion was still angry.

21
00:01:20.825 --> 00:01:23.956
So he stopped a rabbit passing by.

22
00:01:23.957 --> 00:01:26.130
"You there! Stop!

23
00:01:26.131 --> 00:01:30.514
Come here and smell my breath," he ordered.

24
00:01:30.515 --> 00:01:36.224
"Me? Oh yes, my king." The rabbit was scared.

25
00:01:36.225 --> 00:01:41.969
When the lion breathed, she groaned, "Ohh!"

26
00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:49.088
"Does it smell good or bad?" the lion asked.

27
00:01:49.089 --> 00:01:52.737
The rabbit knew that the lion ate the monkey.

28
00:01:52.738 --> 00:01:55.920
So she lied to the lion.

29
00:01:55.921 --> 00:02:03.274
"Oh, my king, your breath smells wonderful."

30
00:02:03.275 --> 00:02:05.581
"Is that so?

31
00:02:05.582 --> 00:02:10.060
How wonderful does it smell?" he asked.

32
00:02:10.061 --> 00:02:19.123
"Umm, uh, your breath smells fruity like an apple," said the rabbit.

33
00:02:19.124 --> 00:02:23.904
"You are lying to me!" growled the lion.

34
00:02:23.905 --> 00:02:28.206
So he ate the rabbit up too.

35
00:02:28.207 --> 00:02:32.216
The fox saw all of this from behind a tree.

36
00:02:32.217 --> 00:02:36.677
He was so terrified that he tried to run away.

37
00:02:36.678 --> 00:02:42.770
"You, little fox," called the lion. "Stop there!"

38
00:02:42.771 --> 00:02:48.227
"Ah . . . oh, yes, my king!" answered the fox.

39
00:02:48.228 --> 00:02:54.584
"Come here and smell my breath," said the lion.

40
00:02:54.585 --> 00:03:00.639
The poor little fox had no choice but to smell the lion's breath.

41
00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:02.901
The lion breathed.

42
00:03:02.902 --> 00:03:07.416
"How was it? Was it good or bad?"

43
00:03:07.417 --> 00:03:12.533
"Umm . . . what should I tell him?" thought the fox.

44
00:03:12.534 --> 00:03:16.180
The lion's breath smelled really bad.

45
00:03:16.181 --> 00:03:18.941
The fox could not lie to him.

46
00:03:18.942 --> 00:03:23.888
But he could not tell the lion what it was really like either.

47
00:03:23.889 --> 00:03:28.462
"Why don't you say something?" the lion asked.

48
00:03:28.463 --> 00:03:33.010
"Do you think my breath smells bad?"

49
00:03:33.011 --> 00:03:40.679
"Oh, no, my king, I, I, uh," said the fox, thinking quickly.

50
00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:42.457
"I have a cold.

51
00:03:42.458 --> 00:03:45.005
Yes, I have a cold!

52
00:03:45.006 --> 00:03:47.533
So my nose is very stuffy.

53
00:03:47.534 --> 00:03:51.382
I cannot smell anything very well," he said.

54
00:03:51.383 --> 00:03:54.681
"I can only guess that your breath smells good.

55
00:03:54.682 --> 00:03:58.500
What do you think?" he asked.

56
00:03:58.501 --> 00:04:07.274
"Ahh, hmm. Yes, I am sure it smells good," said the lion.

57
00:04:07.275 --> 00:04:10.700
"Sure!" agreed the fox.

58
00:04:10.701 --> 00:04:16.447
And the satisfied lion let the fox live.
